comctl32: hide a tracking tooltip when its tool is deleted (TTM_DELTOOL), as Windows does

What he saw (11.10-186, Photoshop 2026, Adobe2026 prefix, 168 dpi): "There is a stale restore dialog that won't go away after
after resizing, but maximizing and unmaximizing works fine" -- the caption button's "Restore" tooltip stays drawn under the
button for good.

Mechanism (SOLID: +tooltips trace of Photoshop, and the source): Photoshop shows its caption-button tips as a TRACKING tooltip
(tooltips_class32, no owner): TTM_ADDTOOLW "Restore", TTM_TRACKPOSITION, TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(TRUE). To take it down it sends
TTM_GETTOOLCOUNT, TTM_DELTOOLW and only then TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE). TOOLTIPS_DelToolT called TOOLTIPS_Hide, which only knows
the non-tracking current tool (nCurrentTool, -1 for a tracking tip) and returned, then reset nTrackTool to -1; the following
TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE) reached TOOLTIPS_TrackHide with nTrackTool == -1 and returned too. No SWP_HIDEWINDOW was ever sent:
the window stayed visible (IsWindowVisible 1) until the next hover reused it. Not a resize issue: in the lab the tip also stays
when the pointer simply leaves the button. Present on 171, 185rc and 186 (upstream Wine code).

Windows (his run of the ttprobe probe, comctl32 6.16): a shown TTF_TRACK tip is hidden right after TTM_DELTOOL (visible=0,
tools=0) and stays hidden after TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE); TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE) with the tool still there hides it as well.

Fix (dlls/comctl32/tooltips.c, built into comctl32.dll AND comctl32_v6.dll): when the deleted tool is the tracked tool,
TOOLTIPS_DelToolT hides the tracking tip through TOOLTIPS_TrackHide (TTN_POP to the tool's window, SWP_HIDEWINDOW) and clears
bTrackActive, before the tool is freed.

Not covered: whether Windows sends TTN_POP on this path was not measured (Wine's existing hide paths send it; Photoshop's tool
has hwnd NULL, so it goes nowhere). TTM_DELTOOL of a tracked tool whose tip is not shown also sends TTN_POP + a hide of an already
hidden window (harmless).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-186tt = 186 + this patch in comctl32.dll x2 + comctl32_v6.dll x2; scratch prefix; desk r6a):
- ttprobe: 186 2/2 "after TTM_DELTOOL visible=1, after TRACKACTIVATE(0) visible=1"; 186tt 2/2 Windows' lines (0, 0, control 0);
  186tt + NEUTRON_TOOLTIP_DELTOOL_HIDE=0 2/2 back to 1, 1.
- Wine's comctl32 tooltips conformance test (tests/tooltips.c, standalone build): 1480 tests, 7 todo, 1 failure (tooltips.c:424
  "got wrong text", resource-less standalone build) identically on 186, 186tt and 186tt + kill switch.
- Photoshop 2026 (fresh PgD-ps2 copies, 168 dpi; hover Restore 3 s, pointer away; hover, click Restore, pointer away, +8 s;
  white "Restore" box pixels at the tip's place): 186tt 3/3 (one with +tooltips) tip drawn while hovering (1699 px), gone after
  leaving and after the restore click (0 px), Wine reports it hidden; kill switch 2/2 stuck (1699 px after leaving/restore, Wine
  visible=1); 186 / 185rc / 171 2/2 each stuck.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_TOOLTIP_DELTOOL_HIDE=0
--- a/dlls/comctl32/tooltips.c	2026-11-09 22:22:52.894700207 -0500
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/tooltips.c	2026-11-09 22:22:52.896954031 -0500
@@ -1181,6 +1181,19 @@
     }
 }
 
+static BOOL neutron_deltool_hide(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        char env[8];
+        DWORD len = GetEnvironmentVariableA( "NEUTRON_TOOLTIP_DELTOOL_HIDE", env, sizeof(env) );
+        on = !(len && len < sizeof(env) && env[0] == '0');
+        TRACE( "NEUTRON_TOOLTIP_DELTOOL_HIDE = %d\n", on );
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static LRESULT
 TOOLTIPS_DelToolT (TOOLTIPS_INFO *infoPtr, const TTTOOLINFOW *ti, BOOL isW)
 {
@@ -1204,6 +1217,17 @@
     /* make sure the tooltip has disappeared before deleting it */
     TOOLTIPS_Hide(infoPtr);
 
+    /* NEUTRON: deleting the tool a tracking tooltip is showing hides the tooltip, as on Windows (comctl32 6.16 measured:
+     * a shown TTF_TRACK tip is hidden right after TTM_DELTOOL, before any TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE)). TOOLTIPS_Hide above
+     * only covers the non-tracking current tool, and the index reset below then made the app's following
+     * TTM_TRACKACTIVATE(FALSE) a no-op: Photoshop 2026's caption-button tip ("Restore") stayed on screen for good.
+     * Kill switch NEUTRON_TOOLTIP_DELTOOL_HIDE=0. */
+    if (nTool == infoPtr->nTrackTool && neutron_deltool_hide())
+    {
+        TOOLTIPS_TrackHide(infoPtr);
+        infoPtr->bTrackActive = FALSE;
+    }
+
     toolPtr = &infoPtr->tools[nTool];
     TOOLTIPS_FreeToolText (toolPtr);
     TOOLTIPS_ResetSubclass (toolPtr);
